default KindPolicy swift_policy = { kind: swift, display_name: "Swift", version_mode: immutable, file_overwrite: refuse, name_case_sensitive: false, has_repository_index: false, signing: none, size_limit: config.limit_size_swift, endpoint_root: "/api/packages/{owner}/swift" }
default KindPolicy vagrant_policy = { kind: vagrant, display_name: "Vagrant", version_mode: additive, file_overwrite: refuse, name_case_sensitive: false, has_repository_index: false, signing: none, size_limit: config.limit_size_vagrant, endpoint_root: "/api/packages/{owner}/vagrant" }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Access derivation and black-box functions
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- can_read_packages(user, registry) / can_write_packages(user, registry):
--   the package access mode of `user` (null = anonymous) on `registry`.
--   from: services/packages/perm.go:16
--   1. Packages disabled, or REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW and anonymous, or the user
--      is inactive / prohibited from logging in: none.
--   2. User-owned registry: the owner has owner access; any other signed-in
--      user has read when the owner is public or limited; anonymous has
--      read when the owner is public. A private user's registry is visible
--      only to that user.
--   3. Organisation registry: a signed-in member gets the highest of the
--      org-wide authorize level of their teams (owners team = owner) and
--      each team's access to the `packages` unit; if that is none and the
--      organisation is visible to the user (public; limited and signed in;
--      private and member) the user gets read.
--   4. Site administrators may do anything (read and write), regardless of
--      the derived mode.
--   5. A request authenticated with a scoped token additionally needs
--      read:package (read) / write:package (write); a public-only token is
--      refused on a private owner's registry. Actions task tokens act with
--      their workflow user's mode.
--   can_read_packages is true for mode >= read; can_write_packages for
--   mode >= write.
--
-- can_write_repo_packages(user, repository) = access/can_write(user, repository, packages)
-- can_read_repo_code(user, repository)      = access/can_read(user, repository, code)
-- is_org_owner(organization, user)          = organizations/is_org_owner(organization, user)
--   (local names because qualified calls cannot be evaluated by the journey walker)
--
-- can_manage_registry(user, registry): the user is the registry's owning
--   user, or an owner of the owning organisation (organizations/
--   is_org_owner). Gates the owner package settings (cleanup rules, Cargo
--   index). from: routers/web/web.go:836, routers/web/web.go:1189
--
-- quota_allows_package_upload(registry): quota/quota_allows(<owner>,
--   size_assets_packages_all), i.e. the QuotaGate gate_package_upload
--   charged to the registry owner (an organisation's quota for org
--   registries), evaluated before the upload is stored.
--   from: routers/api/packages/api.go:96
--
-- same_owner(registry, repository): repository.owner_user = registry.owner_user
--   and repository.owner_org = registry.owner_org.
-- valid_coordinates(kind, name, version, file_name), valid_image_reference
--   (image, reference): per-kind naming rules (see PublishFirstVersionOf-
--   NewPackage guidance); container references are tags or sha256 digests.
-- same_package_name(kind, a, b): equal, case-insensitively unless
--   KindPolicy.name_case_sensitive (Maven). lower(s): lower-cased string.
-- is_semver_kind(kind): versions of this kind follow semantic versioning
--   (cargo, helm, npm, nuget, composer, pub, swift, go ...).
-- extracted_metadata / extracted_*_properties / extracted_image_*(…):
--   what the per-kind parser reads from the uploaded artefact.
-- initial_dist_tags(kind, sha256): npm dist-tags in the publish document.
-- md5_of / sha1_of / sha512_of / blake2b_of(sha256): the other digests of
--   the same content, computed while streaming.
-- is_registry_metadata_file(kind, file_name): Maven maven-metadata.xml and
--   its checksum files under a -SNAPSHOT version.
-- index_scopes_of(registry, kind): the distribution/component/arch (etc.)
--   scopes that currently have packages, plus the one just changed.
-- generated_public_key / generated_chef_public_key: fresh key material.
-- upload_digest_matches(upload, sha256): the digest the client declared
--   equals the digest of the bytes received.
-- manifest_references_resolve(registry, image, sha256): every config and
--   layer blob (or, for an index, every sub-manifest) the manifest names is
--   known to the image (uploaded, mounted or already part of a version).
-- manifest_references_blob(manifest_sha256, blob_sha256), manifest_file_name(sha256):
--   manifest content navigation (the manifest with that digest names the
--   blob with that digest); files are named after their digest.
-- autolink_candidate(package): the repository named by the image source
--   annotation, else label, else by the first image-name segment.
-- blob_readable_by(blob, user): see ContainerMountsBlob guidance.
-- staged_anywhere(blob): some ContainerUploadedBlob refers to the blob.
-- dangling_digest_check(version): see PurgeExpiredPackageData guidance.
-- cleanup_targets_of(rule): see ApplyCleanupRule guidance.
-- latest_of(versions): newest by semver when the package is
--   semver-compatible, else by creation time.
-- stored_size_of / visible_version_count_of / size_sum_of: sums and
--   counts over the registry's files and versions.
-- is_valid_regex(p), is_valid_version_string(s), earliest(a, b): helpers.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Publishing (all kinds except the container blob/manifest flow)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The first upload under a new package name creates the package and its
-- first version.
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:174
rule PublishFirstVersionOfNewPackage {
    when: PublisherUploadsPackageFile(publisher, registry, kind, name, version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    let existing = Package{registry: registry, kind: kind, name: name}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: kind != container
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_coordinates(kind, name, version, file_name)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: not exists existing
    requires: publisher.is_admin or policy.size_limit < 0 or size <= policy.size_limit
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_size < 0 or registry.stored_size + size <= config.limit_total_owner_size
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_count < 0 or registry.visible_version_count < config.limit_total_owner_count
    ensures:
        let package = Package.created(
            registry: registry,
            kind: kind,
            name: name,
            semver_compatible: is_semver_kind(kind),
            is_internal: false,
            repository: null,
            properties: extracted_package_properties(kind, sha256),
            autolink_pending: false
        )
        let new_version = PackageVersion.created(
            package: package,
            creator: publisher,
            version: version,
            created_at: now,
            is_internal: false,
            metadata: extracted_metadata(kind, sha256),
            properties: extracted_version_properties(kind, sha256),
            download_count: 0,
            last_downloaded_at: null,
            is_tagged: false,
            is_yanked: false,
            dist_tags: initial_dist_tags(kind, sha256)
        )
        FileStored(version: new_version, file_name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        PackageVersionCreated(version: new_version, publisher: publisher)
        RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: kind, package: package)
    @guidance
        -- Package names are compared case-insensitively (stored as given)
        -- except Maven, whose group:artifact ids are case-sensitive
        -- (KindPolicy.name_case_sensitive). Version strings always compare
        -- case-insensitively.
        -- valid_coordinates is per kind, e.g. generic: name matches
        -- [-_+.\w]+ (not "..", a single character must be alphanumeric),
        -- filename matches [-_+=:;.()\[\]{}~!@#$%^& \w]+ without surrounding
        -- whitespace and not "."/".."; version has no surrounding
        -- whitespace. npm: (@scope/)?[a-z0-9-][a-z0-9-._]*. PyPI: PEP 440
        -- versions. Cargo: [a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9-_]{0,63}. Swift: scope
        -- [a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,38}, name [a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9-_]{0,99}.
        -- Container image: [a-z0-9]+([._-][a-z0-9]+)*(/...)*. Debian/Arch/
        -- CRAN/NuGet/Composer/Chef/RubyGems/Conan names follow their
        -- ecosystem rules. Metadata is parsed from the artefact itself and an
        -- unparseable artefact is refused.
        -- Site administrators bypass the per-kind size limit and the owner
        -- count/size limits, but not the quota module.
        -- RPM uploads are re-signed with the owner's RPM key when
        -- config.default_rpm_sign_enabled or the uploader asks (?sign=true);
        -- Arch packages uploaded without a detached signature get one made
        -- with the owner's Arch key. Either way the owner key is created on
        -- first need (EnsureSigningKey).
}

-- A new version of a package that already exists.
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:213
rule PublishNewVersionOfExistingPackage {
    when: PublisherUploadsPackageFile(publisher, registry, kind, name, version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    let package = Package{registry: registry, kind: kind, name: name}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: kind != container
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_coordinates(kind, name, version, file_name)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: exists package
    requires: package.is_internal = false
    requires: not exists PackageVersion{package: package, version: version}
    requires: publisher.is_admin or policy.size_limit < 0 or size <= policy.size_limit
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_size < 0 or registry.stored_size + size <= config.limit_total_owner_size
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_count < 0 or registry.visible_version_count < config.limit_total_owner_count
    ensures:
        let new_version = PackageVersion.created(
            package: package,
            creator: publisher,
            version: version,
            created_at: now,
            is_internal: false,
            metadata: extracted_metadata(kind, sha256),
            properties: extracted_version_properties(kind, sha256),
            download_count: 0,
            last_downloaded_at: null,
            is_tagged: false,
            is_yanked: false,
            dist_tags: initial_dist_tags(kind, sha256)
        )
        FileStored(version: new_version, file_name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        PackageVersionCreated(version: new_version, publisher: publisher)
        RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: kind, package: package)
    @guidance
        -- npm: dist-tags supplied with the publish are moved onto the new
        -- version (removed from whichever version held them before).
}

-- Additive kinds accept further files into an existing version
-- (another architecture of a .deb, another wheel, another Vagrant provider,
-- the jar next to the pom, another Conan revision file ...).
-- No PackageVersionCreated is emitted: the version was already published.
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:229
rule AddFileToExistingVersion {
    when: PublisherUploadsPackageFile(publisher, registry, kind, name, version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    let package = Package{registry: registry, kind: kind, name: name}
    let target = PackageVersion{package: package, version: version}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: kind != container
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_coordinates(kind, name, version, file_name)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: exists target
    requires: target.is_internal = false
    requires: policy.version_mode = additive
    requires: not exists PackageFile{version: target, name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key}
    requires: publisher.is_admin or policy.size_limit < 0 or size <= policy.size_limit
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_size < 0 or registry.stored_size + size <= config.limit_total_owner_size
    ensures:
        FileStored(version: target, file_name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: kind, package: package)
    @guidance
        -- Maven checksum uploads (.md5/.sha1/.sha256/.sha512) are not stored:
        -- they are verified against the existing file and acknowledged.
        -- Maven: uploading the .pom (the lead file) also refreshes the
        -- version metadata. maven-metadata.xml at artifact level (no version)
        -- is acknowledged and discarded; under a -SNAPSHOT version it is
        -- stored and replaced on every upload.
}

-- Kinds whose files may be replaced in place (Helm charts, Conan recipe and
-- package files, Arch signatures, Maven snapshot metadata).
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:310
rule ReplaceFileInExistingVersion {
    when: PublisherUploadsPackageFile(publisher, registry, kind, name, version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    let package = Package{registry: registry, kind: kind, name: name}
    let target = PackageVersion{package: package, version: version}
    let old_file = PackageFile{version: target, name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: kind != container
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: exists old_file
    requires: policy.file_overwrite = replace or (policy.file_overwrite = replace_metadata and is_registry_metadata_file(kind, file_name))
    requires: publisher.is_admin or policy.size_limit < 0 or size <= policy.size_limit
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_size < 0 or registry.stored_size + size <= config.limit_total_owner_size
    ensures: not exists old_file
    ensures:
        FileStored(version: target, file_name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: kind, package: package)
    @guidance
        -- When the new content equals the old (same blob) nothing changes.
}

-- Stores content once (deduplicated by hash) and attaches it to a version
-- as a file.
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:283
rule StoreFileContent {
    when: FileStored(version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
    let existing_blob = PackageBlob{hash_sha256: sha256}
    ensures:
        if exists existing_blob:
            PackageFile.created(version: version, blob: existing_blob, name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, created_at: now, properties: extracted_file_properties(version.package.kind, sha256))
        else:
            let blob = PackageBlob.created(size: size, hash_md5: md5_of(sha256), hash_sha1: sha1_of(sha256), hash_sha256: sha256, hash_sha512: sha512_of(sha256), hash_blake2b: blake2b_of(sha256), created_at: now)
            PackageFile.created(version: version, blob: blob, name: file_name, composite_key: composite_key, is_lead: is_lead, created_at: now, properties: extracted_file_properties(version.package.kind, sha256))
    @guidance
        -- All five digests are computed while streaming the upload; the
        -- blob is identified by all of them together. If any later step of
        -- the publish fails, a blob created by this publish is discarded.
}

-- Changes to indexed kinds and to Cargo trigger regeneration of the
-- owner-wide index for that kind.
-- from: routers/api/packages/rpm/rpm.go:216
rule RefreshIndexesAfterChange {
    when: RegistryContentChanged(registry, kind, package)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    ensures:
        if policy.has_repository_index:
            RepositoryIndexStale(registry: registry, kind: kind)
        if kind = cargo:
            CargoIndexEntryStale(registry: registry, package: package)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Repository indexes, signing keys, Cargo index, Chef keys
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/packages/debian/repository.go:101
rule RebuildRepositoryIndex {
    when: RepositoryIndexStale(registry, kind)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    requires: policy.has_repository_index
    ensures:
        for scope in index_scopes_of(registry, kind):
            if exists RepositoryIndex{registry: registry, kind: kind, scope: scope}:
                RepositoryIndex{registry: registry, kind: kind, scope: scope}.built_at = now
            else:
                RepositoryIndex.created(registry: registry, kind: kind, scope: scope, built_at: now)
    ensures:
        if policy.signing != none:
            SigningKeyNeeded(registry: registry, kind: kind)
    @guidance
        -- Debian: Packages(.gz/.xz) per distribution/component/architecture,
        -- Release + InRelease + Release.gpg per distribution, by-hash
        -- addressing. Alpine: APKINDEX.tar.gz per branch/repository/
        -- architecture, RSA-signed. RPM: repomd.xml (+ .asc), primary,
        -- filelists, other per group. ALT: base/ release + pkglist per
        -- group/architecture. Arch: <distribution>.db / .files (+ .sig)
        -- per distribution/architecture, "any" packages appear in every
        -- architecture. A scope with no packages left has its index removed.
        -- The index files live in an internal package/version of the owner
        -- and are never listed or counted.
}

-- from: services/packages/debian/repository.go:42
rule EnsureSigningKey {
    when: SigningKeyNeeded(registry, kind)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    requires: policy.signing != none
    requires: not exists RegistrySigningKey{registry: registry, kind: kind}
    ensures: RegistrySigningKey.created(registry: registry, kind: kind, scheme: policy.signing, public_key: generated_public_key(registry, kind), created_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- The private half is held server side in the owner's settings and
        -- never shown. Debian/RPM/Arch use OpenPGP; Alpine uses RSA.
}

-- Clients fetch the public key to trust the repository; fetching creates
-- the key if the owner has none yet.
-- from: routers/api/packages/debian/debian.go:30
rule ClientFetchesRepositoryKey {
    when: ClientRequestsRepositoryKey(client, registry, kind)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: kind}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_read_packages(client, registry)
    requires: policy.signing != none
    ensures: SigningKeyNeeded(registry: registry, kind: kind)
}

-- from: services/packages/cargo/index.go:109
rule UpdateCargoIndexEntry {
    when: CargoIndexEntryStale(registry, package)
    let index = CargoIndex{registry: registry}
    requires: exists index
    ensures: index.built_at = now
    @guidance
        -- Rewrites the crate's line-delimited JSON file in the index git
        -- repository (one line per version with deps, features, checksum,
        -- yanked flag) as a commit by the acting user. Does nothing if the
        -- owner never initialised the index.
}

-- from: services/packages/cargo/index.go:51
rule OwnerInitializesCargoIndex {
    when: ManagerInitializesCargoIndex(manager, registry)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
    requires: not exists CargoIndex{registry: registry}
    ensures: CargoIndex.created(registry: registry, repository_name: "_cargo-index", built_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- Creates (or reuses) the owner repository `_cargo-index` and writes
        -- config.json: { dl: download URL, api: registry API URL,
        -- auth-required: owner is not public }.
}

-- from: services/packages/cargo/index.go:64
rule OwnerRebuildsCargoIndex {
    when: ManagerRebuildsCargoIndex(manager, registry)
    let index = CargoIndex{registry: registry}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
    requires: exists index
    ensures: index.built_at = now
    @guidance
        -- Removes every crate file and rewrites config.json and one file per
        -- cargo package from current data in a single commit.
}

-- A user creates a new Chef client key pair; the private key is handed to
-- the user once and only the public key is kept.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/packages.go:103
rule UserRegeneratesChefKey {
    when: UserRegeneratesChefKeyPair(user)
    let existing = ChefClientKey{user: user}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            existing.public_key = generated_chef_public_key(user)
            existing.created_at = now
        else:
            ChefClientKey.created(user: user, public_key: generated_chef_public_key(user), created_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- RSA key; the private PEM is returned as a file download named
        -- <user>.priv. Chef clients authenticate by signing requests with it.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Kind-specific version state
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/api/packages/cargo/cargo.go:264
rule CargoYanksVersion {
    when: PublisherYanksCargoVersion(publisher, version)
    let registry = version.package.registry
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: version.package.kind = cargo
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: version.is_yanked = false
    ensures: version.is_yanked = true
    ensures: CargoIndexEntryStale(registry: registry, package: version.package)
}

-- from: routers/api/packages/cargo/cargo.go:264
rule CargoUnyanksVersion {
    when: PublisherUnyanksCargoVersion(publisher, version)
    let registry = version.package.registry
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: version.package.kind = cargo
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: version.is_yanked = true
    ensures: version.is_yanked = false
    ensures: CargoIndexEntryStale(registry: registry, package: version.package)
}

-- Point an npm dist-tag at a version; the tag leaves whichever version of the
-- package held it before.
-- from: routers/api/packages/npm/npm.go:345
rule NpmAddsDistTag {
    when: PublisherSetsNpmDistTag(publisher, version, tag)
    let registry = version.package.registry
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: version.package.kind = npm
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: tag != ""
    requires: not is_valid_version_string(tag)
    ensures:
        for other in version.package.versions:
            if tag in other.dist_tags:
                other.dist_tags.remove(tag)
    ensures: version.dist_tags.add(tag)
}

-- from: routers/api/packages/npm/npm.go:376
rule NpmRemovesDistTag {
    when: PublisherRemovesNpmDistTag(publisher, package, tag)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: package.kind = npm
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, package.registry)
    ensures:
        for v in package.versions:
            if tag in v.dist_tags:
                v.dist_tags.remove(tag)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Container (OCI) registry
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/api/packages/container/container.go:218
rule ContainerStartsBlobUpload {
    when: ContainerClientStartsBlobUpload(publisher, registry, image)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_image_reference(image, "")
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    ensures: BlobUpload.created(registry: registry, image: image, bytes_received: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- A monolithic upload (digest given on the POST) completes in one
        -- request; otherwise an upload session is returned and chunks follow.
}

-- from: routers/api/packages/container/container.go:300
rule ContainerAppendsChunk {
    when: ContainerClientAppendsChunk(publisher, upload, chunk_size)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, upload.registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(upload.registry)
    ensures: upload.bytes_received = upload.bytes_received + chunk_size
    ensures: upload.updated_at = now
    @guidance
        -- Chunks must arrive in order: a chunk whose start offset differs
        -- from bytes_received is refused (range not satisfiable).
}

-- from: services/packages/container/blob.go:49
rule ContainerCompletesBlobUpload {
    when: ContainerClientCompletesBlobUpload(publisher, upload, sha256)
    let registry = upload.registry
    -- read before the upload goes: postconditions see the resulting state
    let image = upload.image
    let bytes = upload.bytes_received
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: container}
    let existing_blob = PackageBlob{hash_sha256: sha256}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: upload_digest_matches(upload, sha256)
    requires: publisher.is_admin or policy.size_limit < 0 or upload.bytes_received <= policy.size_limit
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_size < 0 or registry.stored_size + upload.bytes_received <= config.limit_total_owner_size
    ensures:
        if exists existing_blob:
            ContainerUploadedBlob.created(registry: registry, image: image, blob: existing_blob, uploaded_at: now)
        else:
            let blob = PackageBlob.created(size: bytes, hash_md5: md5_of(sha256), hash_sha1: sha1_of(sha256), hash_sha256: sha256, hash_sha512: sha512_of(sha256), hash_blake2b: blake2b_of(sha256), created_at: now)
            ContainerUploadedBlob.created(registry: registry, image: image, blob: blob, uploaded_at: now)
    ensures: not exists upload
}

-- from: routers/api/packages/container/container.go:395
rule ContainerCancelsBlobUpload {
    when: ContainerClientCancelsBlobUpload(publisher, upload)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, upload.registry)
    ensures: not exists upload
}

-- Cross-repository blob mount: reuse a blob the pusher can already read
-- (in any registry) without re-uploading it.
-- from: services/packages/container/blob.go:110
rule ContainerMountsBlob {
    when: ContainerClientMountsBlob(publisher, registry, image, blob)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: blob_readable_by(blob, publisher)
    ensures: ContainerUploadedBlob.created(registry: registry, image: image, blob: blob, uploaded_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- blob_readable_by: the user is a site admin, or the blob belongs to
        -- a file of a version whose owner is the user, a public or limited
        -- user/org, or an organisation in which the user has at least read on
        -- the packages unit through a team. If the blob is not readable the
        -- client is told to upload it normally instead.
}

-- Deleting a blob by digest removes it from the image's uploaded blobs and
-- from every version of the image that has it as a file.
-- from: services/packages/container/blob.go:166
rule ContainerDeletesBlob {
    when: ContainerClientDeletesBlob(publisher, registry, image, blob)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    ensures:
        for staged in registry.container_uploads:
            if staged.image = image and staged.blob = blob:
                not exists staged
    ensures:
        for f in blob.files:
            if f.version.package.registry = registry and f.version.package.name = image:
                not exists f
}

-- Pushing a manifest (image manifest or image index) under a tag or digest
-- reference publishes that reference as a version of the image package.
-- The first push for an image creates the package and attempts auto-linking.
-- from: services/packages/container/manifest.go:388
rule ContainerPushesManifestForNewImage {
    when: ContainerClientPushesManifest(publisher, registry, image, reference, is_tag, size, sha256)
    let policy = KindPolicy{kind: container}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_image_reference(image, reference)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: not exists Package{registry: registry, kind: container, name: image}
    requires: manifest_references_resolve(registry, image, sha256)
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_count < 0 or registry.visible_version_count < config.limit_total_owner_count
    ensures:
        let package = Package.created(registry: registry, kind: container, name: image, semver_compatible: false, is_internal: false, repository: null, properties: {}, autolink_pending: true)
        let new_version = PackageVersion.created(package: package, creator: publisher, version: reference, created_at: now, is_internal: false, metadata: extracted_image_metadata(sha256), properties: extracted_image_properties(sha256), download_count: 0, last_downloaded_at: null, is_tagged: is_tag, is_yanked: false, dist_tags: {})
        FileStored(version: new_version, file_name: manifest_file_name(sha256), composite_key: null, is_lead: true, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        ContainerManifestLayersAttached(version: new_version, registry: registry, image: image, manifest_sha256: sha256)
        ContainerImageCreated(package: package, publisher: publisher)
        PackageVersionCreated(version: new_version, publisher: publisher)
    @guidance
        -- Schema version must be 2; media type is taken from the request or
        -- the manifest; image index entries must themselves be image
        -- manifests already pushed to this image (each recorded with its
        -- platform os/arch[/variant] and size). Config and layer blobs must
        -- be known to the image. Image config labels/annotations become the
        -- version metadata (description, licenses, source URL, ...).
        -- Reference names are stored lower-cased.
}

-- from: services/packages/container/manifest.go:388
rule ContainerPushesNewReference {
    when: ContainerClientPushesManifest(publisher, registry, image, reference, is_tag, size, sha256)
    let package = Package{registry: registry, kind: container, name: image}
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: valid_image_reference(image, reference)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: exists package
    requires: not exists PackageVersion{package: package, version: reference}
    requires: manifest_references_resolve(registry, image, sha256)
    requires: publisher.is_admin or config.limit_total_owner_count < 0 or registry.visible_version_count < config.limit_total_owner_count
    ensures:
        let new_version = PackageVersion.created(package: package, creator: publisher, version: reference, created_at: now, is_internal: false, metadata: extracted_image_metadata(sha256), properties: extracted_image_properties(sha256), download_count: 0, last_downloaded_at: null, is_tagged: is_tag, is_yanked: false, dist_tags: {})
        FileStored(version: new_version, file_name: manifest_file_name(sha256), composite_key: null, is_lead: true, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        ContainerManifestLayersAttached(version: new_version, registry: registry, image: image, manifest_sha256: sha256)
        PackageVersionCreated(version: new_version, publisher: publisher)
    ensures:
        if package.autolink_pending:
            ContainerImageCreated(package: package, publisher: publisher)
}

-- Re-pushing an existing tag (or digest) re-points it: the old version is
-- replaced by the new manifest; the download count carries over.
-- from: services/packages/container/manifest.go:448
rule ContainerRepointsReference {
    when: ContainerClientPushesManifest(publisher, registry, image, reference, is_tag, size, sha256)
    let package = Package{registry: registry, kind: container, name: image}
    let previous = PackageVersion{package: package, version: reference}
    let carried_downloads = previous.download_count
    let carried_last_download = previous.last_downloaded_at
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, registry)
    requires: quota_allows_package_upload(registry)
    requires: exists previous
    requires: manifest_references_resolve(registry, image, sha256)
    ensures: not exists previous
    ensures:
        let new_version = PackageVersion.created(package: package, creator: publisher, version: reference, created_at: now, is_internal: false, metadata: extracted_image_metadata(sha256), properties: extracted_image_properties(sha256), download_count: carried_downloads, last_downloaded_at: carried_last_download, is_tagged: is_tag, is_yanked: false, dist_tags: {})
        FileStored(version: new_version, file_name: manifest_file_name(sha256), composite_key: null, is_lead: true, size: size, sha256: sha256)
        ContainerManifestLayersAttached(version: new_version, registry: registry, image: image, manifest_sha256: sha256)
        PackageVersionCreated(version: new_version, publisher: publisher)
    @guidance
        -- The superseded manifest's own digest version (if any) is left in
        -- place; it becomes dangling and is purged by the expired-data
        -- cleanup once older than config.cleanup_older_than.
}

-- The config and layer blobs a manifest references become files of the
-- manifest's version and leave the image's uploaded-blob staging area.
-- from: services/packages/container/manifest.go:500
rule AttachManifestLayers {
    when: ContainerManifestLayersAttached(version, registry, image, manifest_sha256)
    ensures:
        for staged in registry.container_uploads:
            if staged.image = image and manifest_references_blob(manifest_sha256, staged.blob.hash_sha256):
                StagedLayerClaimed(version: version, staged: staged)
}

-- A staged upload the manifest references becomes one of the version's files.
-- The blob is read before the staging record goes.
-- from: services/packages/container/common.go:213
rule ClaimStagedLayer {
    when: StagedLayerClaimed(version, staged)
    let blob = staged.blob
    ensures: not exists staged
    ensures: PackageFile.created(version: version, blob: blob, name: manifest_file_name(blob.hash_sha256), composite_key: null, is_lead: false, created_at: now, properties: {})
}

-- Auto-link a new image to a repository: by the
-- org.opencontainers.image.source annotation, else the same label, else by
-- image name "<repo>[/...]" under the same owner. Linking only happens when
-- the pusher could link it by hand. Attempted once per package.
-- from: services/packages/container/manifest.go:585
rule AutolinkContainerImage {
    when: ContainerImageCreated(package, publisher)
    let candidate = autolink_candidate(package)
    requires: package.autolink_pending
    ensures: package.autolink_pending = false
    ensures:
        if candidate != null and package.repository = null and same_owner(package.registry, candidate) and can_write_repo_packages(publisher, candidate):
            package.repository = candidate
    @guidance
        -- The source URL must start with this instance's URL and have the
        -- form <instance>/<owner>/<repo>. Failures are silent.
}

-- Deleting a manifest reference (tag or digest) removes every version of the
-- image matching it.
-- from: routers/api/packages/container/container.go:604
rule ContainerDeletesManifest {
    when: ContainerClientDeletesManifest(publisher, version)
    let package = version.package
    let version_name = version.version
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: package.kind = container
    requires: can_write_packages(publisher, package.registry)
    ensures: not exists version
    ensures: PackageVersionDeleted(version: version, package: package, doer: publisher)
}

-- `docker login` exchange: issue a bearer token for the authenticated user,
-- or an anonymous pull token when sign-in is not required to view.
-- from: routers/api/packages/container/container.go:148
rule ContainerIssuesBearerToken {
    when: ContainerClientRequestsToken(client, credential_expires_at, scope)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: client != null or not config.require_signin_view
    ensures: RegistryBearerToken.created(user: client, scope: scope, issued_at: now, expires_at: earliest(now + config.registry_token_lifetime, credential_expires_at))
    @guidance
        -- The token carries the credential's scope (so a read:package token
        -- stays read-only) and never outlives the credential it was minted
        -- from. Anonymous clients get a token for the ghost user.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Download counting
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/packages/packages.go:707
rule DownloadLeadFileCountsDownload {
    when: ClientDownloadsPackageFile(client, file)
    let version = file.version
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_read_packages(client, version.package.registry)
    requires: file.is_lead
    ensures: version.download_count = version.download_count + 1
    ensures: version.last_downloaded_at = now
    @guidance
        -- Downloading a non-lead file (signature, checksum, layer, index
        -- file) streams it without counting. Web-UI downloads count too.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deletion
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Delete one version with all its files (web settings page, REST API,
-- client protocols: npm unpublish, chef, nuget, debian, rpm, arch, alt,
-- conan, pub/rubygems yank, container manifest delete, site admin).
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:510
rule UserDeletesPackageVersion {
    when: UserRemovesPackageVersion(actor, version)
    let package = version.package
    let registry = package.registry
    let kind = package.kind
    let version_name = version.version
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: version.is_internal = false
    requires: can_write_packages(actor, registry)
    ensures:
        for f in version.files:
            not exists f
    ensures: not exists version
    ensures: PackageVersionDeleted(version: version, package: package, doer: actor)
    ensures: RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: kind, package: package)
    @guidance
        -- RubyGems "yank" and the generic/npm "delete version" endpoints are
        -- deletions. A package left without versions disappears from listings
        -- immediately and is removed by the next expired-data purge.
}

-- Delete every version of a package (npm unpublish-all, chef, conan recipe).
-- from: routers/api/packages/npm/npm.go:295
rule UserDeletesWholePackage {
    when: UserRemovesPackage(actor, package)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: package.is_internal = false
    requires: can_write_packages(actor, package.registry)
    requires: package.visible_versions.count > 0
    ensures:
        for v in package.visible_versions:
            not exists v
            PackageVersionDeleted(version: v, package: package, doer: actor)
    ensures: RegistryContentChanged(registry: package.registry, kind: package.kind, package: package)
}

-- Delete a single file; when it was the last file of its version the version
-- goes too (generic, debian/alpine/rpm/arch per-architecture deletes).
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:534
rule UserDeletesPackageFile {
    when: UserRemovesPackageFile(actor, file)
    let version = file.version
    let package = version.package
    let registry = package.registry
    let version_name = version.version
    let was_last_file = version.files.count = 1
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: version.is_internal = false
    requires: can_write_packages(actor, registry)
    ensures: not exists file
    ensures:
        if was_last_file:
            not exists version
            PackageVersionDeleted(version: version, package: package, doer: actor)
    ensures: RegistryContentChanged(registry: registry, kind: package.kind, package: package)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Linking packages to repositories
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/packages/package_update.go:19
rule UserLinksPackageToRepository {
    when: UserLinksPackage(actor, package, repository)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(actor, package.registry)
    requires: same_owner(package.registry, repository)
    requires: package.repository = null
    requires: can_write_repo_packages(actor, repository)
    ensures: package.repository = repository
}

-- from: services/packages/package_update.go:41
rule UserUnlinksPackageFromRepository {
    when: UserUnlinksPackage(actor, package)
    let repository = package.repository
    let registry = package.registry
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_write_packages(actor, registry)
    requires: repository != null
    requires: can_write_repo_packages(actor, repository)
    requires: actor.is_admin or registry.owner_user = actor or (registry.owner_is_org and is_org_owner(registry.owner_org, actor))
    ensures: package.repository = null
}

-- from: services/repository/delete.go:347
rule RepositoryDeletionUnlinksPackages {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        for p in Packages:
            if p.repository = repository:
                p.repository = null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Owner removal
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Purging a user (admin delete with purge) removes everything in its
-- registry first. No PackageVersionDeleted events are emitted.
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:719
rule PurgeOwnerPackages {
    when: accounts/UserPurged(user)
    let registry = OwnerRegistry{owner_user: user}
    requires: exists registry
    ensures:
        for p in registry.packages:
            for v in p.versions:
                not exists v
    @guidance
        -- Non-purge deletion of a user or organisation is refused while
        -- OwnerRegistry.has_packages (see Requests). Packages, blobs and
        -- leftovers are removed by the next expired-data purge.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cleanup rules (owner settings)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/shared/packages/packages.go:88
rule ManagerCreatesCleanupRule {
    when: ManagerAddsCleanupRule(manager, registry, kind, enabled, keep_count, keep_pattern, keep_last_download_days, remove_days, remove_last_download_days, remove_pattern, match_full_name)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
    requires: not exists CleanupRule{registry: registry, kind: kind}
    requires: keep_count in {0, 1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100}
    requires: remove_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: keep_last_download_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: remove_last_download_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: is_valid_regex(keep_pattern) and is_valid_regex(remove_pattern)
    ensures: CleanupRule.created(registry: registry, kind: kind, enabled: enabled, keep_count: keep_count, keep_pattern: keep_pattern, keep_last_download_days: keep_last_download_days, remove_days: remove_days, remove_last_download_days: remove_last_download_days, remove_pattern: remove_pattern, match_full_name: match_full_name, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- The kind of an existing rule cannot change.
-- from: routers/web/shared/packages/packages.go:88
rule ManagerUpdatesCleanupRule {
    when: ManagerEditsCleanupRule(manager, rule, enabled, keep_count, keep_pattern, keep_last_download_days, remove_days, remove_last_download_days, remove_pattern, match_full_name)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_manage_registry(manager, rule.registry)
    requires: keep_count in {0, 1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100}
    requires: remove_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: keep_last_download_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: remove_last_download_days in {0, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90, 180}
    requires: is_valid_regex(keep_pattern) and is_valid_regex(remove_pattern)
    ensures: rule.enabled = enabled
    ensures: rule.keep_count = keep_count
    ensures: rule.keep_pattern = keep_pattern
    ensures: rule.keep_last_download_days = keep_last_download_days
    ensures: rule.remove_days = remove_days
    ensures: rule.remove_last_download_days = remove_last_download_days
    ensures: rule.remove_pattern = remove_pattern
    ensures: rule.match_full_name = match_full_name
    ensures: rule.updated_at = now
}

-- from: routers/web/shared/packages/packages.go:74
rule ManagerDeletesCleanupRule {
    when: ManagerRemovesCleanupRule(manager, rule)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: can_manage_registry(manager, rule.registry)
    ensures: not exists rule
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Scheduled cleanup
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The `cleanup_packages` cron task: apply every enabled cleanup rule, then
-- purge expired registry data.
-- from: services/cron/tasks_basic.go:145
rule RunScheduledPackageCleanup {
    when: schedule: PackageCleanupSchedule.is_due
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: config.cleanup_enabled
    ensures: schedule.last_run_at = now
    ensures: schedule.next_run_at = now + config.cleanup_interval
    ensures: PackageCleanupRun(older_than: config.cleanup_older_than)
    @guidance
        -- Default schedule "@midnight" and RUN_AT_START = true; modelled as a
        -- fixed interval. Each rule runs in its own transaction and is
        -- retried a few times; a failing rule aborts the task run.
}

-- The same task started by administration (cron dispatch or "run now" on the
-- admin dashboard) with its configured age threshold.
-- from: services/cron/tasks_basic.go:145
rule AdministrationRunsPackageCleanup {
    when: administration/PackageCleanupDue(older_than)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    ensures: PackageCleanupRun(older_than: older_than)
}

-- One cleanup run, however started: apply every enabled cleanup rule, then
-- purge expired registry data older than the threshold.
-- from: services/packages/cleanup/cleanup.go:25
rule RunPackageCleanup {
    when: PackageCleanupRun(older_than)
    ensures:
        for rule in CleanupRules:
            if rule.enabled:
                CleanupRuleDue(rule: rule)
    ensures: ExpiredPackageDataPurgeDue(older_than: older_than)
}

-- from: services/packages/cleanup/cleanup.go:36
rule ApplyCleanupRule {
    when: CleanupRuleDue(rule)
    requires: rule.enabled
    ensures:
        for v in rule.targets:
            for f in v.files:
                not exists f
            not exists v
    ensures: RepositoryIndexStale(registry: rule.registry, kind: rule.kind)
    ensures:
        if rule.kind = cargo:
            for p in rule.registry.packages:
                if p.kind = cargo:
                    CargoIndexEntryStale(registry: rule.registry, package: p)
    @guidance
        -- cleanup_targets_of(rule): for each non-internal package of
        -- rule.kind in rule.registry, walk its non-internal versions newest
        -- first. Container versions named "latest" or named by a digest
        -- (sha256:...) are skipped entirely and not counted. For every other
        -- version, in order:
        --   1. the first keep_count versions are kept (0 = no count keep)
        --   2. the match subject is the version, or "<name>/<version>" when
        --      match_full_name; kept if keep_pattern matches it
        --   3. "last used" = last download, or creation if never downloaded;
        --      kept if last used is within keep_last_download_days
        --   4. kept if created within remove_days
        --   5. kept if last used is within remove_last_download_days
        --   6. kept if remove_pattern is set and does not match
        --   7. otherwise removed.
        -- Patterns are case-insensitive regular expressions that must match
        -- the whole subject. A zero-day window keeps nothing.
        -- Cleanup deletions emit no PackageVersionDeleted events. Index rebuilds
        -- only happen when at least one version was removed.
}

-- Purge leftovers: stale upload sessions, never-referenced container
-- uploads, dangling container digest versions, packages without versions,
-- and blobs no file references. Everything time-based uses older_than.
-- from: services/packages/cleanup/cleanup.go:183
rule PurgeExpiredPackageData {
    when: ExpiredPackageDataPurgeDue(older_than)
    ensures:
        for u in BlobUploads:
            if u.updated_at + older_than <= now:
                not exists u
    ensures:
        for staged in ContainerUploadedBlobs:
            if staged.uploaded_at + older_than <= now:
                not exists staged
    ensures:
        for v in PackageVersions:
            if v.is_dangling_container_digest and v.created_at + older_than <= now:
                not exists v
    ensures:
        for p in Packages:
            if not p.has_versions:
                not exists p
    ensures:
        for b in PackageBlobs:
            if not b.is_referenced and not staged_anywhere(b) and b.created_at + older_than <= now:
                not exists b
    @guidance
        -- A dangling container digest version is one whose version is a
        -- "sha256:" digest, that is not tagged and that no image index
        -- version references. Blob content is removed from storage after the
        -- records are gone.
}

-- Site administrators can run the purge immediately, with no age threshold.
-- from: routers/web/admin/packages.go:102
rule AdminPurgesExpiredDataNow {
    when: AdminRunsPackageDataPurge(admin)
    requires: config.packages_enabled
    requires: admin.is_admin
    ensures:
        for u in BlobUploads:
            not exists u
    ensures:
        for staged in ContainerUploadedBlobs:
            not exists staged
    ensures:
        for v in PackageVersions:
            if v.is_dangling_container_digest:
                not exists v
    ensures:
        for p in Packages:
            if not p.has_versions:
                not exists p
    ensures:
        for b in PackageBlobs:
            if not b.is_referenced and not staged_anywhere(b):
                not exists b
    @guidance
        -- Same purge as PurgeExpiredPackageData with an age threshold of
        -- zero: everything that qualifies is removed now.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/packages/package.go:193
invariant UniquePackageNamePerOwnerAndKind {
    for a in Packages:
        for b in Packages:
            (a != b and a.registry = b.registry and a.kind = b.kind) implies not same_package_name(a.kind, a.name, b.name)
}

-- from: models/packages/package_version.go:31
invariant UniqueVersionPerPackage {
    for a in PackageVersions:
        for b in PackageVersions:
            (a != b and a.package = b.package) implies lower(a.version) != lower(b.version)
}

-- from: models/packages/package_file.go:36
invariant UniqueFilePerVersionAndKey {
    for a in PackageFiles:
        for b in PackageFiles:
            (a != b and a.version = b.version and a.composite_key = b.composite_key) implies lower(a.name) != lower(b.name)
}

-- Content is stored once.
-- from: models/packages/package_blob.go:35
invariant BlobsAreContentAddressed {
    for a in PackageBlobs:
        for b in PackageBlobs:
            a != b implies a.hash_sha256 != b.hash_sha256
}

-- from: models/packages/package_cleanup_rule.go:28
invariant OneCleanupRulePerOwnerAndKind {
    for a in CleanupRules:
        for b in CleanupRules:
            (a != b and a.registry = b.registry) implies a.kind != b.kind
}

-- A package may only be linked to a repository of the same owner.
-- from: services/packages/package_update.go:20
invariant LinkedRepositoryHasSameOwner {
    for p in Packages:
        p.repository != null implies same_owner(p.registry, p.repository)
}

-- Every registry belongs to exactly one owner.
-- from: models/packages/package.go:189
invariant RegistryHasExactlyOneOwner {
    for r in OwnerRegistries:
        (r.owner_user != null) != (r.owner_org != null)
}

-- Internal versions hold registry machinery only and never count.
-- from: models/packages/package.go:281
invariant InternalVersionsAreNeverPublishedByUsers {
    for v in PackageVersions:
        v.is_internal implies v.package.is_internal or v.package.kind = container
}

-- from: services/packages/packages.go:707
invariant DownloadCountNeverNegative {
    for v in PackageVersions:
        v.download_count >= 0
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Anyone who may read the registry (see guidance on PackageBrowsing).
actor PackageReader {
    within: OwnerRegistry
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_packages(this, within)
}

-- Owner, or org member with write on the packages unit, or site admin, acting
-- through a credential that permits package writes.
actor PackagePublisher {
    within: OwnerRegistry
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_write_packages(this, within)
}

-- The user themselves for a user registry; an owner of the organisation for
-- an organisation registry.
actor RegistryManager {
    within: OwnerRegistry
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_manage_registry(this, within)
}

-- Site administrators: access/SiteAdmin.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Package-manager clients talking the per-kind protocol (all kinds except
-- the container registry, which has its own surface).
surface PackageClientProtocol {
    facing client: accounts/User
    context registry: OwnerRegistry

    exposes:
        for p in registry.visible_packages where can_read_packages(client, registry):
            p.name
            p.kind
        for v in PackageVersions where v.package.registry = registry and v.is_internal = false and can_read_packages(client, registry):
            v.version
            v.metadata
            v.is_yanked
            v.dist_tags
        for f in PackageFiles where f.version.package.registry = registry and f.version.is_internal = false and can_read_packages(client, registry):
            f.name
            f.blob.size
            f.blob.hash_sha256
        for i in registry.repository_indexes where can_read_packages(client, registry):
            i.scope
            i.built_at
        for k in registry.signing_keys where can_read_packages(client, registry):
            k.public_key

    provides:
        PublisherUploadsPackageFile(client, registry, kind, name, version, file_name, composite_key, is_lead, size, sha256)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ClientDownloadsPackageFile(client, file)
            when can_read_packages(client, registry)
        ClientRequestsRepositoryKey(client, registry, kind)
            when can_read_packages(client, registry)
        UserRemovesPackageVersion(client, version)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        UserRemovesPackage(client, package)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        UserRemovesPackageFile(client, file)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        PublisherYanksCargoVersion(client, version)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        PublisherUnyanksCargoVersion(client, version)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        PublisherSetsNpmDistTag(client, version, tag)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        PublisherRemovesNpmDistTag(client, package, tag)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)

    @guarantee ScopedCredentialsAreHonoured
        -- A request authenticated with a scoped token needs read:package to
        -- read and write:package to change anything; a token restricted to
        -- public resources is refused on a private owner's registry.
        -- Site administrators bypass the access mode check but not the
        -- token scope check.

    @guarantee LimitsAreReportedDistinctly
        -- Exceeding a per-kind size limit, the owner size limit or the owner
        -- version count is refused as a limit violation; exceeding the quota
        -- module's limit is refused as "quota exceeded"; a duplicate version
        -- or file is refused as a conflict.

    @guidance
        -- Credentials accepted: OAuth2 bearer, access tokens (basic or
        -- bearer), Actions runtime / task tokens, basic auth, reverse proxy
        -- auth; Chef requests signed with the user's ChefClientKey; NuGet
        -- API key; Conan/Swift/Vagrant login handshakes return tokens.
        -- Endpoint roots (under the instance URL, {owner} = registry owner):
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/alpine     key, {branch}/{repo}[/{arch}]
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/alt        {group}.repo, upload, RPMS.*, base/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/arch       repository.key, {distro}/{arch}/...
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/cargo      api/v1/crates, config.json, index paths
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/chef       api/v1/universe|search|cookbooks
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/composer   packages.json, p2/, files/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/conan      v1/ and v2/ (ping, users, conans, files)
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/conda      {channel}/{subdir}/repodata.json, uploads
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/cran       src/contrib, bin/{platform}/contrib/{rversion}
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/debian     repository.key, dists/, pool/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/generic    {name}/{version}/{filename}
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/go         upload, module proxy paths
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/helm       index.yaml, {filename}, api/charts
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/maven      {group path}/{artifact}/{version}/{file}
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/npm        {id}, @{scope}/{id}, -/package/.../dist-tags, -/v1/search
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/nuget      index.json, query, registration/, package/, symbols/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/pub        api/packages/versions/new, {id}
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/pypi       upload POST /, simple/{id}, files/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/rpm        repository.key, {group}.repo, upload, repodata/, package/
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/rubygems   specs, info/, gems/, api/v1/gems
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/swift      {scope}/{name}[/{version}], identifiers, login
        --   /api/packages/{owner}/vagrant    authenticate, {name}/{version}/{provider}
        -- Discovery endpoints (NuGet service index, Swift login, Vagrant
        -- authenticate, Conan ping) answer without authentication so clients
        -- can negotiate.
}

-- The OCI distribution API served at /v2.
surface ContainerRegistryProtocol {
    facing client: accounts/User
    context registry: OwnerRegistry

    exposes:
        for p in registry.visible_packages where p.kind = container and can_read_packages(client, registry):
            p.name
        for v in PackageVersions where v.package.registry = registry and v.package.kind = container and v.is_tagged and can_read_packages(client, registry):
            v.version
        for staged in registry.container_uploads where can_read_packages(client, registry):
            staged.blob.hash_sha256
            staged.blob.size
        for u in BlobUploads where u.registry = registry and can_write_packages(client, registry):
            u.bytes_received

    provides:
        ContainerClientRequestsToken(client, credential_expires_at, scope)
        ContainerClientStartsBlobUpload(client, registry, image)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientAppendsChunk(client, upload, chunk_size)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientCompletesBlobUpload(client, upload, sha256)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientCancelsBlobUpload(client, upload)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientMountsBlob(client, registry, image, blob)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientDeletesBlob(client, registry, image, blob)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientPushesManifest(client, registry, image, reference, is_tag, size, sha256)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ContainerClientDeletesManifest(client, version)
            when can_write_packages(client, registry)
        ClientDownloadsPackageFile(client, file)
            when can_read_packages(client, registry)

    @guarantee SignedInClientsOnly
        -- Every /v2 request other than the token exchange needs a signed-in
        -- user or a registry bearer token; an anonymous bearer token is
        -- issued only when the instance does not require sign-in to view.

    @guidance
        -- GET /v2 (support check), GET /v2/token, GET /v2/_catalog (images
        -- the caller can read, max config.container_list_max per page),
        -- /v2/{owner}/{image}/blobs/uploads[/{uuid}] (POST/GET/PATCH/PUT/
        -- DELETE, ?mount=&from=), /v2/{owner}/{image}/blobs/{digest}
        -- (HEAD/GET/DELETE), /v2/{owner}/{image}/manifests/{reference}
        -- (PUT/HEAD/GET/DELETE), /v2/{owner}/{image}/tags/list (?n=&last=).
        -- Image names may contain "/" segments.
}

-- Web UI and REST API (/api/v1/packages/{owner}) read views of a registry.
surface PackageBrowsing {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context registry: OwnerRegistry

    exposes:
        registry.has_packages when can_read_packages(viewer, registry)
        for p in registry.visible_packages where can_read_packages(viewer, registry):
            p.name
            p.kind
            p.properties
            p.latest_version
        for p in registry.visible_packages where p.repository != null and can_read_packages(viewer, registry) and can_read_repo_code(viewer, p.repository):
            p.repository
        for v in PackageVersions where v.package.registry = registry and v.is_internal = false and can_read_packages(viewer, registry):
            v.version
            v.creator
            v.created_at
            v.metadata
            v.properties
            v.download_count
            v.last_downloaded_at
            v.total_size
            v.is_tagged
            v.dist_tags
            v.is_yanked
        for f in PackageFiles where f.version.package.registry = registry and f.version.is_internal = false and can_read_packages(viewer, registry):
            f.name
            f.created_at
            f.properties
            f.blob.size
            f.blob.hash_md5
            f.blob.hash_sha1
            f.blob.hash_sha256
            f.blob.hash_sha512
        for policy in KindPolicies:
            policy.display_name
            policy.endpoint_root
            policy.name_case_sensitive

    provides:
        ClientDownloadsPackageFile(viewer, file)
            when can_read_packages(viewer, registry)

    related:
        PackageVersionSettings(registry)
            when can_write_packages(viewer, registry)

    @guarantee VisibilityFollowsOwner
        -- Reading a registry depends only on its owner, never on a linked
        -- repository: a public owner's packages are readable by everyone
        -- (anonymous included unless sign-in is required to view), a
        -- limited owner's by every signed-in user, a private user's only by
        -- that user, a private organisation's only by its members.
        -- Linking a package to a private repository does not hide it;
        -- the linked repository is only shown to viewers who can read it.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /{owner}/-/packages (latest version of each package; filter
        -- by kind and name; paging config.packages_paging_num),
        -- /{owner}/-/packages/{kind}/{name} (redirects to latest version),
        -- .../versions (container: tagged / untagged filter; sort by name,
        -- version, created, size), .../{version} (install instructions per
        -- kind, metadata, properties, files, other versions, download count,
        -- linked repository), .../{version}/files/{fileid} (download).
        -- REST: GET /api/v1/packages/{owner} (?type=&q=, paged),
        -- GET /api/v1/packages/{owner}/{type}/{name}/{version},
        -- GET .../{version}/files. Also faces the anonymous visitor (see
        -- access) with the same can_read_packages guard.
}

-- What a package writer can do with one package from the web UI and REST API.
surface PackageVersionSettings {
    facing writer: accounts/User
    context registry: OwnerRegistry

    exposes:
        for p in registry.visible_packages where can_write_packages(writer, registry):
            p.repository

    provides:
        UserLinksPackage(writer, package, repository)
            when can_write_packages(writer, registry)
        UserUnlinksPackage(writer, package)
            when can_write_packages(writer, registry)
        UserRemovesPackageVersion(writer, version)
            when can_write_packages(writer, registry)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /{owner}/-/packages/{kind}/{name}/{version}/settings (link to
        -- a repository of the same owner, delete this version).
        -- REST: DELETE /api/v1/packages/{owner}/{type}/{name}/{version},
        -- POST /api/v1/packages/{owner}/{type}/{name}/-/link/{repo_name},
        -- POST /api/v1/packages/{owner}/{type}/{name}/-/unlink.
        -- All REST writes require a token with write:package.
}

-- Owner-level package settings: cleanup rules, Cargo index, Chef key.
surface OwnerPackageSettings {
    facing manager: accounts/User
    context registry: OwnerRegistry

    exposes:
        for rule in registry.cleanup_rules where can_manage_registry(manager, registry):
            rule.kind
            rule.enabled
            rule.keep_count
            rule.keep_pattern
            rule.keep_last_download_days
            rule.remove_days
            rule.remove_last_download_days
            rule.remove_pattern
            rule.match_full_name
            rule.targets
        for index in registry.cargo_index where can_manage_registry(manager, registry):
            index.repository_name
            index.built_at
        for key in ChefClientKeys where key.user = manager and registry.owner_user = manager:
            key.public_key

    provides:
        ManagerAddsCleanupRule(manager, registry, kind, enabled, keep_count, keep_pattern, keep_last_download_days, remove_days, remove_last_download_days, remove_pattern, match_full_name)
            when can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
        ManagerEditsCleanupRule(manager, rule, enabled, keep_count, keep_pattern, keep_last_download_days, remove_days, remove_last_download_days, remove_pattern, match_full_name)
            when can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
        ManagerRemovesCleanupRule(manager, rule)
            when can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
        ManagerInitializesCargoIndex(manager, registry)
            when can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
        ManagerRebuildsCargoIndex(manager, registry)
            when can_manage_registry(manager, registry)
        UserRegeneratesChefKeyPair(manager)
            when registry.owner_user = manager

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/packages[/rules/add | /rules/{id} |
        -- /rules/{id}/preview | /cargo/initialize | /cargo/rebuild |
        -- /chef/regenerate_keypair] and
        -- /org/{org}/settings/packages[/rules/... | /cargo/...] (org owners).
        -- The preview lists rule.targets without deleting anything.
}

-- A repository's "Packages" tab lists packages linked to it.
surface RepositoryPackages {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        for p in Packages where p.repository = repository and p.is_internal = false and can_read_repo_code(viewer, repository):
            p.name
            p.kind
            p.latest_version

    @guidance
        -- Web: /{owner}/{repo}/packages (latest version per linked package,
        -- filter by kind / name). Shown as a tab when the repository's
        -- `packages` unit is enabled.
}

-- Site administration of the registry.
surface SiteAdminPackages {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    exposes:
        for v in PackageVersions:
            v.version
            v.package.name
            v.package.kind
            v.total_size
            v.created_at
        for b in PackageBlobs:
            b.size
            b.is_referenced

    provides:
        UserRemovesPackageVersion(admin, version)
        AdminRunsPackageDataPurge(admin)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /admin/packages (all non-internal versions, filter by kind and
        -- name, sort; total referenced and unreferenced blob size),
        -- POST /admin/packages/delete, POST /admin/packages/cleanup.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred KindProtocols.wire_formats    -- see: detailed/package-protocols.allium (one adapter per kind; endpoint roots on PackageClientProtocol)
deferred RepositoryIndex.file_formats  -- see: detailed/package-repository-indexes.allium (Debian/Alpine/RPM/ALT/Arch layouts)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "The web settings page links a package to any repository of the same owner without checking the user's write access to that repository and without requiring the package to be unlinked first, while the REST API checks both. The spec adopts the API behaviour for both; confirm."
open question "Unlinking requires the actor to be a site admin, the owning user, or an organisation owner, on top of package write access; linking only needs package write and repository write. Is this asymmetry intended?"
open question "The cleanup-rule form renders keep/remove last-download-days fields but never binds them, so they cannot be set from the UI today. The spec lets managers set them; confirm they should be user-editable."
open question "A token restricted to public resources is refused only for private owners; limited owners are allowed. Should 'public only' also exclude limited owners?"
open question "Actions workflow tokens can publish to the repository owner's registry with the owner's package permissions (marked TODO in Forgejo). Should they be narrowed to the workflow's own repository / linked packages?"
open question "Owner count/size limits (LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_*) and the quota module overlap. Should a rebuild keep both mechanisms or express the LIMIT_* settings as default quota rules?"
open question "Dangling container digest versions are purged only by the expired-data cleanup; cleanup rules deliberately skip them and the 'latest' tag. Keep this split?"
open question "Owner deletion: users/orgs are refused deletion while they own packages unless purged; org purge does not exist. Should organisation deletion also be able to purge packages?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST accounts/UserPurged(user): emitted when an admin deletes a user with purge; packages removes the user's registry content.
-- REQUEST accounts/owns_packages(user): answer with packages/OwnerRegistry{owner_user: user}.has_packages (non-internal versions exist); refuse non-purge deletion while true.
-- REQUEST accounts/UserRenamed: no package reaction needed; image and registry coordinates are derived from the owner's current name.
-- REQUEST organizations/Organization.deletion: refuse deletion while packages/OwnerRegistry{owner_org: org}.has_packages.
-- REQUEST organizations/is_org_owner(org, user): used by can_manage_registry and unlinking.
-- REQUEST organizations/TeamUnitAccess for unit `packages`: needed to derive can_read/can_write_packages for org registries (max of team authorize level and team packages-unit access).
-- REQUEST repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer): already emitted; packages unlinks linked packages.
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository: creating the `_cargo-index` repository on behalf of the owner (OwnerInitializesCargoIndex).
-- REQUEST can_write_repo_packages(user, repository) and can_read_repo_code(user, repository): used for linking and for showing linked repositories.
-- REQUEST access/config.require_signin_view: imported as config.require_signin_view (used by can_read_packages and the container token exchange).
-- REQUEST authentication/TokenScope: read:package / write:package and public-only flag consumed by can_read/can_write_packages.
-- REQUEST quota/quota_allows(owner, size_assets_packages_all) (QuotaGate gate_package_upload, charged: package_owner): quota_allows_package_upload(registry) is exactly this, evaluated for the registry owner (not the uploader) before every write that stores data; quota/QuotaUsage.packages should sum packages/PackageFile sizes per owner (blob shared by two files counts twice, as LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_SIZE does).
-- REQUEST webhooks, actions: react to PackageVersionCreated(version, publisher) / PackageVersionDeleted(version, package, doer) with exactly these parameter names.
